@@ -207,6 +207,17 @@ contiguous window); a read outside it returns no vertex and the batch is dropped
 All calls come from the NV2A poll thread, one at a time, so a back end can
 create its window and device lazily and pump messages from `flip`.
 
+P8 texture metadata includes the programmed 32, 64, 128 or 256 palette
+entries; zero in a caller-constructed `Nv2aTexture` means the previous
+256-entry default. Out-of-range indices are rejected, not wrapped or used to
+read past that range. The CPU rasterizer uses its existing failed-sample
+fallback; whole-texture P8 decoding reports failure without changing the
+output. `nv2a_backend_decode_p8_data` accepts explicit source, palette and
+output extents for stable caller-owned snapshots. On Windows the guest-memory
+whole-texture decoder also rejects inaccessible pages without consuming a
+guard. These checks do not determine undocumented NV2A out-of-range behaviour
+or discover an unreported suballocation boundary.
+
 Things a back end should get right. These come from a Direct3D 11 back end
 written against this interface for one title; that back end is not in this
 tree, so treat them as advice from one implementation, not as tested behaviour
